  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on computing an aspiration level (2250) and comparing each outcome to it, then favoring the lottery with the higher chance of exceeding it. This involves explicit comparison of outcomes to a mean-based reference point and attention to which outcomes surpass it. In contrast, the individual's report focuses on avoiding losses and does not reference any calculation of an average outcome or aspiration level. The justification is loss-minimization, not aspiration-seeking. There is no mention of the 3000 or 6000 outcomes relative to a computed benchmark, nor any indication that the individual evaluated which lottery more frequently exceeds a mental reference point. The reasoning is more consistent with loss aversion or minimax-type logic than with the aspiration-level rule described. Therefore, while both the reason and the individual may end up favoring Lottery A, the cognitive process differs. The information used and the justification do not align with the aspiration-level reason.",
